steps.instruction:
Prepare five standard solutions for each dye group at the following concentrations (mg L⁻¹):
- Amaranth, Ponceau 4R, Carmoisine, Ponceau SX, Erythrosine, Sudan IV: 1.0, 2.5, 5.0, 10.0, 20.0;
- Allura Red AC, Ponceau 3R, Sudan I, Sudan II, Sudan III: 0.5, 1.0, 2.5, 5.0, 10.0;
- Carmine: 5, 10, 20, 40, 80.
Inject each standard (10 µL) under the HPLC conditions above to generate calibration curves.
